Package: openbox
Architecture: any
Depends:
    ${shlibs:Depends},
    ${misc:Depends},
    python3-openbox,
    openbox-themes
Recommends:
    openbox-menu,
    openbox-xdg-autostart
Suggests:
    tint2 | fbpanel | lxpanel,
    conky,
    feh | nitrogen
Description: standards-compliant, fast, light-weight and extensible window manager
 Openbox is a window manager for the X11 windowing system. It is designed to be
 small, fast, and fully compliant with the Inter-Client Communication
 Conventions Manual (ICCCM) and Extended Window Manager Hints (EWMH).
 .
 Openbox 4 is a complete rewrite in Rust, featuring:
  - Memory safety and improved performance
  - CSS-based theming with dark mode support
  - D-Bus IPC for modern desktop integration
  - Extension API for plugins
  - Python bindings for automation
  - xdg-desktop-portal support

Package: openbox-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends:
    openbox (= ${binary:Version}),
    ${misc:Depends}
Description: development files for Openbox
 This package contains the header files and static library for developing
 Openbox extensions and plugins.

Package: python3-openbox
Section: python
Architecture: any
Depends:
    ${python3:Depends},
    ${misc:Depends},
    python3-dbus,
    python3-gi
Description: Python bindings for Openbox
 This package provides Python bindings for controlling Openbox via D-Bus,
 including scripting support with Lua.

